{"body":"## Documentation\r\n\r\n- [`I14.6`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-06-durable-work-admission-and-execution-axes.md#i146-durable-work-admission-and-execution-axes) — I14.6. Durable work, admission and execution axes\r\n- [`I14.8`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-08-fair-and-portfolio-aware-scheduling.md#i148-fair-and-portfolio-aware-scheduling) — I14.8. Fair and portfolio-aware scheduling\r\n- [`I14.20`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-20-canonical-runtime-lifecycle-vocabulary.md#i1420-canonical-runtime-lifecycle-vocabulary) — I14.20. Canonical runtime lifecycle vocabulary\r\n\r\n## Contract requires\r\n\r\nAdmission and execution are separate axes. Kernel must stage an inactive `AdmissionReservation` in ORS, record canonical `ADMITTED` plus launch outbox, then activate that exact reservation using the matching canonical admission receipt, unchanged State Fence, and Authority Epoch. A process may launch only from an **active** matching reservation with an activation receipt. A staged reservation may reduce capacity but may not provision, launch, or cause an external effect.\r\n\r\n## Code today\r\n\r\nThe inventory identifies Kernel-local ORS storage for `AdmissionReservation` and launch-related code in `eliot-kernel/src/dispatch_launch.rs` and `src/daemon_process_launch.rs`, plus admission clients in `eliot-native-worker/src/kernel_admission_client.rs` and `eliotd/src/dreamer_admission.rs`. The measured facts establish that Kernel is the sole durable writer and that eliotd polls and claims work under a one-second lease, but they do not establish the required three-step ORS-stage → canonical-admit/outbox → ORS-activate saga or prove that launch is gated by an activation receipt.\r\n\r\n## Consequence\r\n\r\nA launch path cannot be shown to have a durable, fenced authority boundary. Crashes between capacity reservation, canonical admission, and process launch can produce unaccounted capacity claims, launches without canonical authority, duplicate effects, or a durable object that is semantically admitted without an active reservation.\r\n\r\n## Work\r\n\r\nIn `eliot-kernel`, define or complete a single Kernel-owned admission transition that:\r\n  - creates a stable `reservation_id` and proposed attempt ID;\r\n  - stages `AdmissionReservation::STAGED_INACTIVE` in ORS with the full resource, lane, environment, effect, quota, State Fence, and Authority Epoch claims;\r\n  - commits canonical work admission as `ADMITTED` and writes the launch outbox with the canonical admission receipt reference;\r\n  - activates only that reservation identity after validating the canonical receipt, State Fence, and Authority Epoch;\r\n  - persists an activation receipt and requires it in every process/provider launch path;\r\n  - reuses the reservation identity across crash recovery and retry;\r\n  - releases or expires reservations through a receipt, while forbidding cleanup expiry for an active reservation attached to a nonterminal attempt.\r\n  Make `dispatch_launch.rs`, `daemon_process_launch.rs`, and every provider/worker dispatch path reject launch when the reservation is staged, missing, mismatched, released, expired, or reconciling.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria\r\n\r\nA submitted work item visibly progresses through `READY → ADMITTED`, has one persisted reservation first visible as `STAGED_INACTIVE`, then one matching activation receipt, and only then creates a run attempt entering `PROVISIONING`. Restarting Kernel after canonical admission but before activation reuses the same reservation ID and produces no launched process. Attempting to invoke any launch path with only a canonical admission or only an ORS staged reservation is rejected with preserved operation identity and evidence.\r\n\r\n## Scope and owner\r\n\r\n- Owner: `eliot-kernel`\r\n- Severity: blocking\r\n- Kind: unprovable\r\n\r\nTests are minimal by owner order: add only the smallest proof named under acceptance. No test campaigns, no fixture matrices.\r\n\r\n---\r\nFiled by the root controller from a section-by-section conformance audit of I14 (queueing, backpressure and degraded behaviour) against the implementation contract. The audit report is kept at `.swarm/runs/20260912T115840Z/reports/`.","labels":[],"state":"OPEN","title":"[I14-audit] Implement the normative admission reservation saga before any launch"}
