{"body":"## Documentation\r\n\r\n- [`I14.2`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-02-default-queue-profiles.md#i142-default-queue-profiles) — I14.2. Default queue profiles\r\n- [`I14.3`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-03-control-reserve.md#i143-control-reserve) — I14.3. Control Reserve\r\n- [`I14.4`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-04-backpressure-responses.md#i144-backpressure-responses) — I14.4. Backpressure responses\r\n- [`I14.5`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-05-recovery-directive.md#i145-recovery-directive) — I14.5. Recovery Directive\r\n- [`I14.11`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-11-canonical-store-outage.md#i1411-canonical-store-outage) — I14.11. Canonical store outage\r\n- [`I14.12`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-12-memory-pressure.md#i1412-memory-pressure) — I14.12. Memory pressure\r\n- [`I14.1`](https://github.com/UnknownAlienHuman/eliot-memory-os/blob/main/docs/architecture/I14-01-work-classes.md#i141-work-classes) — I14.1. Work classes\r\n\r\n## Contract requires\r\n\r\nControl capacity must be independently reserved at every applicable bottleneck: Kernel control channel and runnable task slots, ORS write budget and durable bytes, store transaction slots and pending-write memory, process launch/termination, notifications, CPU and protected memory, pipe bytes, handles/file descriptors, and disk queue capacity. Admission must evaluate the exact exhausted resource vector, preserve control/recovery work, shed or defer normal/background work, and name both exhausted resource and affected work. Every rejection/degradation response must use a defined disposition and include every `RecoveryDirective` field. A preallocated last-resort control slot must record reserve exhaustion or establish a platform/manual-recovery boundary.\r\n\r\n## Code today\r\n\r\nThe repository has control-plane and runtime components in `eliot-kernel/src/control_plane.rs`, `src/daemon_runtime.rs`, `src/canonical_store_runtime.rs`, launch code in `src/dispatch_launch.rs`, and notification functionality in `eliot-notify`. The inventory and measured facts do not identify queue profiles, `runtime.toml` defaults, per-resource reserve accounting, a last-resort control slot, or a uniform `RecoveryDirective` contract.\r\n\r\n## Consequence\r\n\r\nThe implementation cannot prove that cancellation, fencing, safe shutdown, health, critical incident transitions, or recovery remain possible during resource exhaustion. Generic queue-full or transport failures can lead callers to retry unsafe operations, while a saturated normal lane can starve the work needed to restore safety.\r\n\r\n## Work\r\n\r\nIn `eliot-kernel`, implement a centrally owned pressure/admission subsystem with typed resource dimensions at least for CPU task slots, protected memory, ORS operation count/bytes, canonical-store write/transaction capacity, process-control capacity, pipe/message bytes, handles, and disk queue bytes. Add default profile values to `runtime.toml` for all I14.1 pools, including the specified defaults for interactive, verification, canonical writes, background, and reports.\r\n  - Reserve control capacity independently from normal capacity at each relevant resource.\r\n  - Prevent interactive, normal, background, model, and swarm work from borrowing reserved control capacity.\r\n  - Make each admission outcome include the exhausted dimensions, affected work class, whether work was shed/deferred/quarantined, and the next permissible action.\r\n  - Define and serialize all I14.4 dispositions: `BUSY`, `STORAGE_BACKPRESSURE`, `ACCEPTED_PENDING`, `DB_UNAVAILABLE`, `BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`, `STATE_CHURN`, and `CAPABILITY_DEGRADED`.\r\n  - Attach a complete `RecoveryDirective` to each disposition, including commit status, preservation status, retry or poll instruction, forbidden actions, fallback, escalation condition, and resolution state.\r\n  - Preallocate a last-resort Kernel control record/slot outside normal resource accounting. If it cannot be used, transition explicitly to the platform/manual-recovery boundary rather than silently failing.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria\r\n\r\nWhen normal work exhausts ORS durable bytes, a normal submission returns `STORAGE_BACKPRESSURE` with a complete `RecoveryDirective`, while a cancellation/control record can still be persisted through the reserved control capacity. When CPU or handle capacity alone is exhausted, normal/background admission is independently closed and the response names that precise resource; control/recovery admission remains available until its own reserve is exhausted. If the dedicated final control slot is unavailable, the system emits an explicit manual/platform-recovery state rather than reporting ordinary queue pressure.\r\n\r\n## Scope and owner\r\n\r\n- Owner: `eliot-kernel`\r\n- Severity: blocking\r\n- Kind: missing\r\n\r\nTests are minimal by owner order: add only the smallest proof named under acceptance. No test campaigns, no fixture matrices.\r\n\r\n---\r\nFiled by the root controller from a section-by-section conformance audit of I14 (queueing, backpressure and degraded behaviour) against the implementation contract. The audit report is kept at `.swarm/runs/20260912T115840Z/reports/`.","labels":[],"state":"OPEN","title":"[I14-audit] Add multidimensional control reserves and named backpressure dispositions"}
